course: dictionary
lesson: 11281
title: Who is a writer?
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A writer is a person who writes books, stories, poems, articles or scripts, often as their job. The word can also mean anyone who has written a particular thing, such as the writer of a note or a letter. The ending -er shows that a writer is someone who does writing.
explain: «The end was indeed nearer than even the Rat suspected.» Here the writer warns us that something is coming. The writer chose these words on purpose, so the reader feels that danger is close.
explain: When you read like a writer, ask why the author chose a word, how the first line hooks you, and how tension builds. Writers make choices, and you can make them too. Some writers write in a certain way, such as a funny writer or a writer of spooky stories.
fact: A writer is a person who writes books, stories, poems, articles or scripts.
fact: Roald Dahl and Beverly Cleary are famous writers of children's books.
fact: Jean-Michel Basquiat started as a graffiti writer in New York and painted in the 1980s. He became famous young and died at 27.
fact: A writer can also be anyone who has written a particular thing, such as the writer of a letter.
fact: Writers are needed in big games too, as well as in books.
exercise: «The end was indeed nearer than even the Rat suspected.» What is the writer doing here? | *Warning the reader that something is coming | Telling a joke about rats | Saying the story has finished | Asking the reader a question
exercise: Jean-Michel Basquiat started as a graffiti writer in New York. What kind of writer was he at the start? | A writer of games for phones | *A writer who painted words and pictures on walls | A writer of school reports | A writer of recipe books
exercise: Which word means a person who writes books, stories, poems, articles or scripts, often as a job? | Painter | *Writer | Editor | Reader
test: Which two famous people are named as children's writers in this lesson? | Basquiat and the Rat | *Roald Dahl and Beverly Cleary | Jean-Michel Basquiat and the Buddha | Dahl and Basquiat
test: The writer of «a note» means what? | Someone who reads the note | Someone who lost the note | The paper the note is on | *Someone who has written the note
exam: Why does a writer choose words carefully? | *To make the reader feel and understand what they want to tell them | To make the sentence longer | Because the reader cannot read well | To fill up the page
